---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

// Written to describe what is TRUE TODAY, not a boilerplate policy for a site
// that collects things this one does not. The advertising and analytics
// sections are clearly marked as future state; when either goes live they move
// into the present tense and the date is bumped. Claiming to use advertising
// cookies before any exist would be a false statement in a legal document.

const structuredData = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE.url}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy', item: `${SITE.url}/privacy` },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy | QuickOper"
  description="QuickOper is a static site with no backend. Calculator inputs never leave your device, there is no account, and nothing you type is transmitted, logged or stored."
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <article class="text-ink-soft space-y-4">
    <h1 class="text-ink text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>

    <p class="text-ink-mute text-sm">Last updated {SITE.legalLastUpdated}.</p>

    <div class="border-line bg-sunken rounded-panel border p-4">
      <p class="text-ink font-semibold">The short version</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Nothing you type into a calculator ever leaves your device. There is no account,
        no sign-up, and at present no cookies and no analytics of any kind.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      What happens to what you type
    </h2>

    <p>
      Nothing. QuickOper is a static site: the pages are files, and the calculators are
      JavaScript that runs on your own machine after the page has loaded. Your balances,
      rates and payments are processed entirely in your browser's memory.
    </p>

    <p>
      This is not a policy commitment we could quietly break — it is how the site is
      built. There is no server-side application and no database, so there is nothing that
      could receive your figures even if we wanted it to. The source is public at
      <a class="text-brand underline" href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener">GitHub</a> if you would
      like to check.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Shareable links</h2>

    <p>
      When you change a calculator's inputs, the web address updates so you can bookmark
      the result or send it to someone. That address is built and read in your browser; it
      is not transmitted to us.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong class="text-ink">The link carries figures, never names.</strong> Balances, interest
      rates and minimum payments are encoded; the labels you give your debts are not. A link
      you paste into a forum, a screenshot or an email therefore shows the numbers and never
      who you owe money to. This is deliberate.
    </p>

    <p>
      Anyone you send the link to can see the figures in it, so treat it as you would any
      other message containing personal detail.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Downloads and printing
    </h2>

    <p>
      Spreadsheet exports and printable documents are generated in your browser from data
      already on your screen. Nothing is uploaded in order to produce them, and we never
      see the file.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Cookies and local storage
    </h2>

    <p>
      QuickOper currently sets <strong class="text-ink">no cookies</strong> and writes nothing
      to your browser's storage. If that changes, this page will say so before it happens and
      the date above will be updated.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Server logs</h2>

    <p>
      The site is served by Cloudflare, which processes standard request information —
      including your IP address — in order to deliver pages and protect against attack.
      That is a normal function of any web host, and it applies to the request for the
      page, not to anything you enter into a calculator. Cloudflare acts as our hosting
      provider and handles that data under its own terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      Analytics and advertising — not yet in use
    </h2>

    <div class="border-line rounded-panel border border-dashed p-4">
      <p>
        <strong class="text-ink">
          Neither of the following is live today. This section describes what we intend to
          introduce, so the change is not a surprise.
        </strong>
        When either is switched on, this page will be updated and this notice removed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="pt-2">
      <strong class="text-ink">Analytics.</strong> We plan to measure how many people visit
      which pages, using a cookieless method that does not identify individuals or follow them
      between sites. Calculator inputs will never be included in any measurement — an event
      may record that a calculation was completed, never what was calculated.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong class="text-ink">Advertising.</strong> The site may later carry advertising supplied
      by <strong class="text-ink">Google</strong>, including through Google AdSense.
      Google and its partners use cookies and similar technologies to serve and measure
      adverts, and may use information about your visits to this and other sites to show
      adverts relevant to you.
    </p>

    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
      <li>
        Google's use of advertising cookies is described in its
        <a
          class="text-brand underline"
          href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads"
          rel="noopener">advertising policies</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can opt out of personalised advertising in
        <a
          class="text-brand underline"
          href="https://myadcenter.google.com/"
          rel="noopener">Google's ad settings</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        Visitors in the UK and EU will be asked for consent before any advertising or
        measurement cookie is set, through a certified consent tool.
      </li>
      <li>
        Advertising will never influence what a calculator returns. The arithmetic does
        not know what is on the page beside it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Children</h2>

    <p>
      QuickOper is intended for adults and is not directed at children under 13. We do not
      knowingly collect information from anyone, of any age.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Your rights</h2>

    <p>
      Data protection law gives you rights to access, correct and erase personal data held
      about you. In practice we hold none: there are no accounts, no mailing list and no
      stored calculator inputs. If you have emailed us, we hold that correspondence and
      will delete it on request.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-ink pt-6 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>

    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a
        class="text-brand underline"
        href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a
      >, or see <a class="text-brand underline" href="/contact">contact</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
